# Runtime and HTTP

**Status:** current. `@log` is **planned**.

Owner: generated dispatch in `rocci-cli` (`dispatch.rs`) plus lowering in
`rocci-template`. Custom `main.roc` apps skip this dispatcher.

## Handler matrix

| Declaration | Method | Success | Datastar | Ordinary client | Route |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `@get:view(path)` | GET | `text/html` document | load/navigation | same | authored path |
| `@get:fragment(path)` | GET | fragment | finite `datastar-patch-elements` | same SSE body | authored path |
| `@post:fragment(path)` and mutation variants | POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE | fragment | finite `datastar-patch-elements` | same SSE body | authored path |
| `@post:command(path)` and mutation variants | POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE | `{}` | finite empty SSE, no morph | `204 No Content` | authored path |
| `@get:live(path)` | GET | fragment | poll stream; skip unchanged HTML | event-stream | authored path |

The closed matrix rejects GET commands and non-GET views/live routes.
Duplicate method/path pairs conflict across the assembled app. Discriminate
Datastar with `Datastar-Request: true`, not `Accept`. Successful commands have
no JSON representation: Datastar receives HTTP 200 finite empty SSE, while an
ordinary client receives HTTP 204.

Complete examples: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

## Request access

Generated calls are `handler!(context, request)`. Read the body, headers, and
route data from `request` when the handler lists that parameter.

## Standalone lifecycle

1. `@init` — failure exits the process
2. Listen on loopback (`rocci.toml` / `--port`)
3. Own state in `@context` (typically SQLite)
4. Dispatch normalized document / fragment / command / live routes
5. `?` in handlers → HTTP 500 (HTML overlay for Datastar; error representation otherwise)
6. Shutdown with the process

Every `@get:live(path)` becomes an SSE route, including live routes from
sibling modules. That GET is a long-lived EventSource. Generated live is
a **timer poll**, not write-triggered push: each connection re-renders
every 100 ms and emits `datastar-patch-elements` only when HTML bytes
change. A keepalive is a **separate** unnamed SSE frame so the host 30s
idle timeout does not close a quiet stream. It must not run at poll
rate. Each subscription owns its own connection and poll loop.
A document receives an automatic `data-init=@get(path,
[OpenWhenHidden(True)])` only when its module has exactly one live route and
the body has no authored `data-init`. With multiple streams, subscribe
explicitly.

## Datastar asset

Pinned JS is staged under `/assets`. Version comes from `[assets].datastar`
or `rocci datastar pin`. Upstream expression language:
[data-star.dev](https://data-star.dev/). Rocci documents only what it generates
or pins.

## Assets, health, logging

`/assets` serves application files. Generated `/health` exists for smoke
checks. `pf.Stderr.line!` is teed to the CLI and Dev Console under `rocci run`.
Do not log from `@component`. There is no `@log`.

Environment: `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_PORT`, `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_HOST` (container
override; not a `rocci.toml` field), `DB_PATH` in examples, `ROCCI_CONFIG`.

**Related:** [Server declarations](/docs/reference/language/server/), [CLI run](/docs/reference/cli/#run).
